        "is_free": false,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🧠 Welcome to &quot;<u><i><strong>The Incredible Number Puzzles</strong></i></u>&quot; -- the ultimate test for your numerical skills and mathematical knowledge! Whether you're looking for a serious challenge or a fun way to sharpen your mind, this game is the perfect practice tool💪.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game features four distinct challenge types, each carefully designed to test a different aspect of your mathematical ability🔎.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Linear</strong>: 🎯<i>Construction &amp; Strategy</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Twisted</strong>: 💡<i>Numerical Sense &amp; Logic</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzle 24</strong>: 🔢<i>Mental Math</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Four 4s</strong>: ✨<i>Creativity</i></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Linear&quot; is a fun and challenging math game. You can produce numbers, operators from factories, then pick them up from storages and place into appropriate space of a formula on the top, hopefully its result same as the targeted answer.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Twisted&quot; provides you a formula, but a few numbers or operators are missing or swapped. Use your keen numerical sense to identify and correct the errors to complete the equation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The &quot;24 puzzle&quot; is a mental math puzzle. You need to use all given <strong>4 integers exactly once</strong> to work out 24, by only using ➕ ➖ ✖️ ➗<strong> and ( )</strong>. For example, 4, 5, 8, 8, a possible solution is (5+8÷8)×4=24. Top tip: 4 × 6, 3 × 8 and 2 × 12 all equal to 24.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The &quot;Four 4s&quot; challenge is an old math problem. You need to use <strong>exactly four 4s</strong> and basic math operations to work out a given numbers.On top of normal four operations, you can also use <strong>square roots, factorials, decimals, and repeating decimals</strong>. For example, 44÷4-4=7.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We hope you enjoy these challenges🚀! Remember, it is <strong>never too young nor too old</strong> to learn and enjoy the power of mathematics. 💯</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🧠 Welcome to &quot;<u><i><strong>The Incredible Number Puzzles</strong></i></u>&quot; -- the ultimate test for your numerical skills and mathematical knowledge! Whether you're looking for a serious challenge or a fun way to sharpen your mind, this game is the perfect practice tool💪.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game features four distinct challenge types, each carefully designed to test a different aspect of your mathematical ability🔎.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Linear</strong>: 🎯<i>Construction &amp; Strategy</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Twisted</strong>: 💡<i>Numerical Sense &amp; Logic</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Puzzle 24</strong>: 🔢<i>Mental Math</i></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Four 4s</strong>: ✨<i>Creativity</i></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Linear&quot; is a fun and challenging math game. You can produce numbers, operators from factories, then pick them up from storages and place into appropriate space of a formula on the top, hopefully its result same as the targeted answer.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&quot;Twisted&quot; provides you a formula, but a few numbers or operators are missing or swapped. Use your keen numerical sense to identify and correct the errors to complete the equation.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The &quot;24 puzzle&quot; is a mental math puzzle. You need to use all given <strong>4 integers exactly once</strong> to work out 24, by only using ➕ ➖ ✖️ ➗<strong> and ( )</strong>. For example, 4, 5, 8, 8, a possible solution is (5+8÷8)×4=24. Top tip: 4 × 6, 3 × 8 and 2 × 12 all equal to 24.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The &quot;Four 4s&quot; challenge is an old math problem. You need to use <strong>exactly four 4s</strong> and basic math operations to work out a given numbers.On top of normal four operations, you can also use <strong>square roots, factorials, decimals, and repeating decimals</strong>. For example, 44÷4-4=7.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >We hope you enjoy these challenges🚀! Remember, it is <strong>never too young nor too old</strong> to learn and enjoy the power of mathematics. 💯</p>",
        "short_description": "Attention Math Geniuses (and those who just think they are)! Throw away your calculators, because this is the game where your so-called &quot;brilliant numeric skills&quot; and &quot;encyclopedic maths knowledge&quot; are about to get a serious reality check. Let's whip those rusty brain gears into shape!",
